"listopad" has a hemisphere bias, as do other non-Latin and non-number name=
s=20
of Gregorian months. "pavmasti" would collide with non-Roman calendars, in=
=20
which the first month is at different times of the year. As the Gregorian=
=20
calendar is the fourth version of the Roman calendar, I thought it fitting =
to=20
take the names of the months from Latin, though the forms of the words are=
=20
taken from various languages ("ianvari" is from Russian, "madjio" is from=
=20
Italian) or from no particular language. A quick check of Wiktionary shows =
a=20
large plurality, possibly a majority, of languages using Latin-derived word=
s=20
for month names.

